      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "FORMS:\n- Predicate: {愛|あい}らしい\n- Modifier: {愛|あい}らしい + noun\n- Adverbial: {愛|あい}らしく\n- Noun form: {愛|あい}らしさ (loveliness, charm)\n\nUSAGE:\n{愛|あい}らしい is a more refined and literary alternative to かわいい. It implies a gentle, delicate charm that inspires affection. Often used for small children, small animals, flowers, and other things that evoke tenderness.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {愛|あい}らしい: lovely, endearing (refined, literary quality)\n- かわいい: cute (everyday, broad usage)\n- {愛|いと}おしい: dear, precious (deeper emotional attachment)\n- {可憐|かれん}な: sweet, delicate (emphasizes fragile beauty)",
